{"input -> load -> Document.parse -> include:: processor -> File.open/OpenURI.open_uri": {"user_controlled": "yes", "evidence": "The filter’s call method passes @text (user input) directly into Asciidoctor.convert, so attacker-supplied markup reaches the parser and include processor.", "trace": ["lib/banzai/filter/asciidoc_filter.rb:L36-L38", "lib/banzai/filter/asciidoc_filter.rb:L73-L75"]}, "options[:to_file] -> convert logic -> doc.normalize_system_path -> doc.write": {"user_controlled": "no", "evidence": "The asciidoc_opts hash passed to Asciidoctor.convert is defined as a literal and does not include a to_file key, so users cannot inject it.", "trace": ["lib/banzai/filter/asciidoc_filter.rb:L62-L70"]}, "options[:to_dir] -> convert logic -> doc.normalize_system_path & Helpers.mkdir_p -> doc.write": {"user_controlled": "no", "evidence": "AsciidocFilter builds asciidoc_opts without a to_dir option, preventing user influence over the output directory.", "trace": ["lib/banzai/filter/asciidoc_filter.rb:L62-L70"]}, "options[:mkdirs] -> convert logic -> Helpers.mkdir_p": {"user_controlled": "no", "evidence": "No mkdirs option is set in asciidoc_opts, so directory creation behavior cannot be controlled by the input.", "trace": ["lib/banzai/filter/asciidoc_filter.rb:L62-L70"]}, "options[:attributes]['templatesdir'] -> TemplateConverter.scan -> Tilt::Template.load -> template.render (ERB)": {"user_controlled": "yes", "evidence": "Asciidoctor.convert is invoked on user markup without restricting custom attributes, so a document header may define :templatesdir: to control template lookup.", "trace": ["lib/banzai/filter/asciidoc_filter.rb:L62-L70", "lib/banzai/filter/asciidoc_filter.rb:L73-L75"]}, "options[:attributes]['stylesheet']/['copycss']/['stylesdir'] -> convert logic -> doc.normalize_system_path -> doc.read_asset & File.write": {"user_controlled": "yes", "evidence": "User-defined AsciiDoc attributes like :stylesheet: can be included in the input, influencing asset rea